title: 'a-clock: iOS + Android scaffolds and responsive mobile layout'
summary: 'Extended a-clock from macOS to mobile using Tauri 2, reusing the same React frontend. Scaffolded iOS (gen/apple Xcode project) and Android (gen/android Gradle project) targets and installed their Rust targets. Refactored src-tauri/src/lib.rs to gate desktop-only features (menu-bar tray, hide-on-close, pmset wake) under #[cfg(desktop)] so the mobile builds compile. Confirmed the app builds and runs in the iOS Simulator (full UI, notification permission prompt fired). Converted the desktop sidebar into a responsive bottom tab bar with safe-area insets and clamped fonts via a max-width:640px media query — mobile look, identical functionality. Freed disk (cleared Xcode DerivedData) to unblock the toolchain.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#tauri-core'
files_created:
  - src-tauri/gen/apple (iOS Xcode project)
  - src-tauri/gen/android (Android Gradle project)
files_modified:
  - src-tauri/src/lib.rs
  - src/App.css
  - index.html
decisions:
  - id: tauri-mobile
    decision: Target iOS and Android with Tauri 2, reusing the React frontend, rather than native or Flutter
    rationale: User asked for Android compatibility and the simplest build. Tauri 2 wraps the same web UI for both mobile platforms, so the entire app ports with near-zero code changes; only the alarm-firing mechanism needs platform-native rework.
  - id: cfg-desktop-gating
    decision: 'Gate tray, hide-on-close, and pmset wake under #[cfg(desktop)] / #[cfg(target_os = macos)]'
    rationale: Those APIs and the tray-icon feature are desktop/macOS-only; without gating, the iOS and Android Rust builds fail to compile.
  - id: css-only-mobile-layout
    decision: Make the layout responsive with a CSS media query (sidebar -> bottom tab bar) instead of restructuring components
    rationale: The user wanted a mobile look while keeping the bones of how the app works. A pure-presentation breakpoint changes zero behavior and benefits iOS and Android identically.
learnings:
  - 'Tauri desktop-only APIs (tray::*, window hide/close, the tray-icon cargo feature) must be #[cfg(desktop)]-gated or the mobile targets won''t compile.'
  - tauri ios dev builds all Rust crates for the iOS arch (~2 min first pass) then xcodebuild + launches on a chosen simulator; success shows '** BUILD SUCCEEDED **' and an 'Info connection' line when the app connects to the dev server.
  - Mobile dev needs real disk headroom (iOS+Android Rust targets, pods, gradle); a full disk fails CocoaPods with 'No space left on device'.
  - env(safe-area-inset-*) needs viewport-fit=cover in the viewport meta to take effect on iOS.
